A||||6||gtsonly||fuel pump keeps running||||5||
Z||000000||gtsonly||11-22-2000||06:19 PM||||what does it mean when your fuel pump keeps running even after you turn your car off. my friends car is doing that right now and it won't start.<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-22-2000||07:05 PM||||it will normally run untill the oil pressure fall off. if it runs beyond that either the FP relay is bad or the oil pressure sender is bad.<P>as to why it won't start.... did you check for spark yet? did you check fuel pressure?||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||11-22-2000||07:32 PM||||As for the fuel pump, I'd bet money on the relay.  It's located in the engine bay, on the firewall behind the driver seat.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||11-23-2000||08:19 AM||||I'd bet on the oil pressure switch keeping the fuel pump running. Pull the three wire connector off and if the pump stops, it's a bad switch. These things fail in the closed position. <P>Ogre, I think he means it wont start because the pump runs until the battery is dead.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||11-23-2000||12:35 PM||||I'll second (or third) the presure sender/switch. I've replaced several for that problem. Running-on for a minute is normal if the oil is thick and you start the car and shut it off before the oil heats up. Beyond that, the switch in the sender is FUBAR.||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||11-23-2000||06:11 PM||||I had the same prob not too long ago. Replace you oil sending unit (yes it runs the fuel pump)...its around 25 bucks and a VERY easy fix. Pull the fuel pump fuse for a temp fix of battery drain.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rockcrawl||11-23-2000||07:31 PM||||An easier temporary fix (if it is in fact a bad oil pressure switch) is to just leave the switch unplugged. The car will still operate normally, you won't even know it's disconnected.||||reg||1
